# claude-seat-1: task 1790632440 ("A deal that leaves fewer than two seats able to act runs the board out, and the clock never folds a seat that cannot act")

Closes: 1790632440 (done)

## What landed (branch claude/seat-1, on top of main c773fca)

- d114a0a fix: a deal that leaves fewer than two seats able to act runs the board out, and the clock never folds a seat that cannot act (E-106, review gap 4; task 1790632440)
  - src/table_canister/src/lib.rs: `start_new_hand`'s in-lock body is now `pub fn deal_hand(state, deck, &proof, now)` (post antes and blinds, deal, set `action_on`, NO clock) and `pub fn open_the_action(state, now)`, with this hand's history push between them. The order matters: `record_local_hand_result` writes the LAST history entry and `reveal_seed_on_hand_end` looks its entry up by hand number, so a settlement inside the deal had to follow the push or it would have written this hand's result into the previous hand's record. Same message, no await between the steps.
  - `open_the_action`: when `the_posts_closed_the_betting(state)` (fewer than two seats can act AND none of them owes a call) it runs the board out through `advance_to_next_street`, the rule that function already applies at every later street; otherwise it arms the clock exactly as before. The second clause is a refinement of the task's one-line rule: heads-up with the big blind all-in for 15 and the small blind holding 1,000, ONE seat can act and it owes 5, so it must be asked (test `a_deal_that_leaves_one_seat_owing_a_call_still_asks_it`, green before and after).
  - `resolve_expired_action_timer`: after the `hand_in_progress` guard, a clock pointed at a seat for which `!can_still_act` is dropped and the hand is moved on through `advance_game` (a closed round runs the board out; an open one moves the clock to the next seat that can act). Returns `None`: nobody timed out, no fold, no timeout charged. This is what heals a table dealt on the old engine and upgraded mid-hand. It routes through `advance_game`, so task 1790632441's executor (leave_table on action) should know the clock path now reaches `advance_game` from one more place.
  - No settlement arithmetic changed; the run-out is the existing path. Saturating arithmetic unchanged. No check weakened. No Candid change (`deal_hand`, `open_the_action` are host-test `pub fn`s, not canister methods; `table_canister.did` untouched). No TableState field added.
  - src/table_canister/tests/betting_rules.rs section 6: six tests on the REAL deal (`deal_hand` + `open_the_action` over a stacked deck), asserting the WINNER, not conservation: heads-up both posts all-in; ante table where the antes take everyone all-in (layered side pots by hand strength); one seat owing a call is asked; the only seat that can act and owes nothing gets its uncalled 15 back and the board runs out; the clock never folds an all-in seat (three-handed, action moves on, the seat stays eligible for the nuts); a clock left pointing at an all-in seat heads-up runs the board out.
  - docs/DEFECTS.md: E-106 (high, FIXED, task 1790632440) register row and write-up naming the gate. docs/CODEBASE-REVIEW-2026-09-28.md gap 4's "Register: not recorded" now points at E-106.

